Bundled SeVim diagram engine
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

The ``sevim/`` sub-package is a separately citable scientific
contribution.  Work that uses the SeVim pipeline directly
(``tools/build_sevim_diagrams``, ``viz/render``, the math-semantic
graph builder under ``sevim/math_graph*.py``) should ALSO cite SeVim:

    Kermani Kolankeh, A. and Zgheib, R. (2026).
    "SeVim: Deterministic Semantic-to-Visual Mapping for Real-Time
     Diagram Generation via Hybrid Neuro-Symbolic Reasoning."
    Zenodo preprint, doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20011107.

See ``sevim/README.md`` and ``sevim/CITATION.cff`` for the standalone
description.

